sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch02-02: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.81" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.813"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Diameter and height for hundreds of thousands of trees are already in open allometric tables, and a log-log comparison with the rival exponents 1 and 2 is a standard regression. That decides the scaling law that is the core of the claim, including the relative slenderness of smaller stems. The single-pine height of about 300 ft needs a modulus the density database does not supply, and several mechanical models can share an exponent, but neither gap blocks a clear test of the stated 3/2 relation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Regress log stem diameter on log height. An exponent near 3/2 would support elastic similarity; exponents near 1 or 2 would favor geometric similarity or constant-stress scaling instead. The separate numerical cap of about 300 ft is checked by inserting the measured taper, density, and modulus of a pine of the Kew-flagstaff form into Greenhill's buckling formula." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Inventories are cross-sectional, so young-versus-old slenderness is inferred from size rather than from followed stems.", "Wind and hydraulics predict exponents similar to elastic buckling, and elastic modulus is not in the density table." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch02-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--operationalizability> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch02-02--grok--data-existence> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
